    AllowKernelInitialization->False]],
  DefaultBaseStyle->"NetworkGraphics",
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,
  FrameTicks->None,
  ImageSize->560]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"63017de4-e893-934f-bd45-\
0b23ce911e84"],

Cell["\<\
At quadratic order, quotienting by linear field redefinitions removes \
directions that act directly on the kinetic operator itself, including simple \
rescalings. That is mathematically legitimate but usually not the desired \
equivalence relation for the kinetic term. The toolkit therefore keeps \
quadratic sectors modulo IBP only.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"98ff24c3-85aa-5641-ab17-d2fb19132934"],

Cell["Relation to Gauge Invariance", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d564356a-2ac7-474d-8244-e8883da83df6"],

Cell["\<\
The toolkit does not automatically impose linearized diffeomorphism \
invariance. Its quotients are by total derivatives and field redefinitions, \
not by gauge symmetry. This is why the off-shell quadratic four-derivative \
space is larger than the curvature-squared gauge-invariant subspace.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b30b90bd-43fa-3443-bd75-86eed1104443"],

Cell["Why the Validation Matters", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"664e141f-a78e-3a4a-ae1f-365ada3c74c7"],

Cell["\<\
The reducer has been tested on expanded Lagrangians that are known to be of \
the form E_FP^{mu nu} Delta h_{mu nu}. The strongest stored test builds such \
an expression in sector {3,4}, expands it to 240 scalar terms, and still \
reduces it to exactly zero. That confirms that the implemented image quotient \
matches the mathematical one in a genuinely nontrivial case.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"28146f7f-b6c6-d249-9d7f-eebbf39870d6"],

Cell["Takeaway", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b26be1c0-0918-ea45-9fb7-da94956623fa"],

Cell["IBP reduction is a kernel quotient.", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3a56e57b-d894-ef4b-9153-bd8f8211e86f"],

Cell["Field-redefinition removal is an image quotient.", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"8eb548ba-b477-7b4f-a9a5-d3cd9d279977"],

Cell["\<\
The toolkit is a sector-wise linear algebra realization of those two facts.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"1bd88f83-0975-874f-ad8a-9637a46c8a2c"]
},
